  "body": "## Goal\nAdopt the approved Base v9.1 operating-system architecture without changing product code, scenes, game data, assets, balance, or player-facing rules.\n\n## Required contract\n- One canonical `skills/PROJECT_BASE_ADAPTER.json`\n- Generated `skills/PROJECT_SKILL_SNAPSHOT.json`\n- Thin repository-discovered workflow router under `.agents/skills/`\n- Separate `docs/PROJECT_OPERATING_HEALTH.json` and generated operating dashboard\n- Base shared Skill bodies remain in Base; project-specific Skills and canon remain local\n- Operating maturity and product-evidence maturity remain separate\n- Compatibility views are generated and marked, never hand-edited\n- GitHub/implementation truth precedes Google Sheet synchronization\n\n## Acceptance\n- RED/GREEN evidence for new or edited Skill behavior and adapter tooling\n- Existing and new repository tests pass\n- JSON, links, routing, hashes, aliases, protected paths, generated views, `git diff --check`, and repository integrity pass\n- P0/P1 adversarial findings are zero\n- Runtime, device, accessibility, and human evidence remain explicit PASS/FAIL/NOT_RUN/NOT_APPLICABLE\n- Protected product paths have zero changes\n- Draft PR only; no automatic merge\n\n## Project-specific boundaries\n- Route shared Foundation/Specialist responsibilities to Base.\n- Keep only current project-owned core-design, Godot planning, UX, and art routes active.\n- Classify inactive legacy Skills conservatively; preserve vertical-slice/product-not-started boundary.",
